## 4. Register the handler **before** any `MapView` is created

```kotlin
package com.example.maplibrevault

import android.app.Application
import org.maplibre.android.MapLibre
import org.maplibre.android.MapLibreOptions

class MyApp : Application() {

    override fun onCreate() {
        super.onCreate()

        // -----------------------------------------------------------------
        // 1️⃣  Build the MapLibreOptions and plug in our handler
        // -----------------------------------------------------------------
        val options = MapLibreOptions()
            .httpRequestHandler(VaultRequestHandler())

        // -----------------------------------------------------------------
        // 2️⃣  Initialise the SDK with those options
        // -----------------------------------------------------------------
        MapLibre.getInstance(this, options)
    }
}
```

> **Important** – The SDK **must** be initialised *once* (usually in `Application.onCreate`) **before** you inflate any `MapView` or `MapFragment`. If you call `MapLibre.getInstance()` a second time the call is ignored, so make sure the handler is set the first time.

